<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.3.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02122</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.3.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>099060ef-7e2c-4d85-baf8-e6b2e7dbc580</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will begin to solve quadratic equations by reasoning about what values would make the equations true and by using structure in the equations. You will explore in depth the idea that some quadratic equations have two solutions.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Find solutions to quadratic equations by reasoning about the values that make the equation true.</item>
        <item>Explain that quadratic equations may have one or two solutions.</item>
        <item>Implement the square root property.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>8.3.1: Determining the Number of Solutions</item>
        <item>8.3.2: Recognizing Pairs of Solutions <list id="list-00003">
            <item>8.3.2: Self Check</item>
            <item>8.3.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>
        <item>8.3.3: Solving More Complex Quadratic Equations <list id="list-00004">
            <item>8.3.3: Self Check</item>
            <item>8.3.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>
        <item>8.3.4: Finding the Solutions</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00005">
        <item>8.3.5: Practice</item>
        <item>8.3.6: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
